WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:03.340
Roxy arrived at the construction site in the mountains.

2
00:00:03.341 --> 00:00:06.740
Detective Smith stood in front of the big, bronze door.

3
00:00:06.741 --> 00:00:08.602
It was still closed.

4
00:00:08.603 --> 00:00:11.265
"Hey, Detective!" Roxy said.

5
00:00:11.266 --> 00:00:14.531
"Did you ring the doorbell to see if anyone's—?"

6
00:00:14.532 --> 00:00:18.271
"Shh!" Detective Smith put a finger to his lips.

7
00:00:18.272 --> 00:00:19.794
He looked scared.

8
00:00:19.795 --> 00:00:21.639
Roxy held up her hands.

9
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.310
"Okay, okay," she whispered.

10
00:00:24.311 --> 00:00:26.838
"Did you try opening the door?"

11
00:00:26.839 --> 00:00:28.537
The detective shook his head.

12
00:00:28.538 --> 00:00:30.263
"I don't know what's in there.

13
00:00:30.264 --> 00:00:33.729
But it's quiet now, and I want to keep it that way."

14
00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.383
"Well, we probably need to know what's in there."

15
00:00:37.384 --> 00:00:40.326
Roxy pushed on the door, but it didn't budge.

16
00:00:40.327 --> 00:00:45.257
"Grr!" Roxy pushed again. The door still wouldn't open.

17
00:00:45.258 --> 00:00:49.612
"Hmph!" Roxy said. "Stand back, Detective."

18
00:00:49.613 --> 00:00:53.227
Whiz-hoo! Roxy fired her eye laser beams.

19
00:00:53.228 --> 00:00:55.814
They bounced off the door and shot right back at her.

20
00:00:55.815 --> 00:01:00.194
"Yikes!" Roxy ducked, and the beams hit a huge boulder.

21
00:01:00.195 --> 00:01:01.734
The boulder exploded.

22
00:01:01.735 --> 00:01:06.285
"Whoa!" Detective Smith said. "That door is strong!"

23
00:01:06.286 --> 00:01:08.204
Roxy stared at the door.

24
00:01:08.205 --> 00:01:10.939
Orange beams radiated from her eyes.

25
00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.551
She expected the door to heat up and melt.

26
00:01:13.552 --> 00:01:15.949
But that didn't happen.

27
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.792
Next she used her freeze breath.

28
00:01:19.793 --> 00:01:22.409
That had no effect on the door either.

29
00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:26.945
"I can't believe this." Roxy moaned.

30
00:01:26.946 --> 00:01:29.628
"I'm the most powerful person on Earth.

31
00:01:29.629 --> 00:01:32.420
And I can't even open a door!"

32
00:01:32.421 --> 00:01:36.126
"What about your x-ray vision?" Detective Smith said.

33
00:01:36.127 --> 00:01:39.319
"Maybe you can at least see what's on the other side."

34
00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:45.694
"Good idea." Roxy stared at the door again.

35
00:01:45.695 --> 00:01:50.293
"There's a tunnel that goes down, but it's really long and really dark.

36
00:01:50.294 --> 00:01:54.745
I can't see where it goes." She sighed. "It's

37
00:01:54.746 --> 00:01:56.757
no use, Detective. I

38
00:01:56.758 --> 00:01:59.997
can't open the door or see what made the noise." She

39
00:01:59.998 --> 00:02:08.009
tapped her chin. "But I know someone who can—maybe." ***

40
00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:10.570
"Okay, Cozlin," Febby said.

41
00:02:10.571 --> 00:02:13.717
"What would you buy if you had a million partecs?"

42
00:02:13.718 --> 00:02:16.043
Cozlin and her friends were out at recess.

43
00:02:16.044 --> 00:02:17.683
They were playing zip disk.

44
00:02:17.684 --> 00:02:21.076
"I don't know." Cozlin ran with the disk.

45
00:02:21.077 --> 00:02:24.577
"I guess a new suspension pool would be fun."

46
00:02:24.578 --> 00:02:27.134
She took a shot at the goal and missed.

47
00:02:27.135 --> 00:02:28.820
Mert got the disk.

48
00:02:28.821 --> 00:02:33.438
"You don't need a million partecs to buy a suspension pool."

49
00:02:33.439 --> 00:02:36.677
He tried to take a shot, but Drupp stole the disk.

50
00:02:36.678 --> 00:02:41.459
"What would you buy with a million partecs, Drupp?" Cozlin asked.

51
00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:45.918
Drupp ran across the court. "I'd buy a space ski."

52
00:02:45.919 --> 00:02:47.633
Mert rolled his eyes.

53
00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:52.906
"You don't need a million partecs for a space ski either."

54
00:02:52.907 --> 00:02:57.780
Drupp sent the disk zipping into the goal.

55
00:02:57.781 --> 00:03:01.024
"You do if it's a hyperspace ski!"

56
00:03:01.025 --> 00:03:05.449
Everyone laughed.

57
00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.433
Cozlin's watch beeped.

58
00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:11.837
"I'll be right back. I'm . . . thirsty!"

59
00:03:11.838 --> 00:03:17.579
She stepped away and opened her watch.

60
00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:21.685
"Hey, Roxy!" Cozlin smiled. "What's up?"

61
00:03:21.686 --> 00:03:25.935
Roxy frowned. "I've got a big problem."

62
00:03:25.936 --> 00:03:30.146
"Is a big monster destroying Metro City?" Cozlin asked.

63
00:03:30.147 --> 00:03:32.549
"Are robots invading Earth?"

64
00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.287
Roxy shook her head.

65
00:03:34.288 --> 00:03:37.910
"Don't laugh, but there's a door I can't open."

66
00:03:37.911 --> 00:03:39.675
Cozlin scratched her head.

67
00:03:39.676 --> 00:03:42.899
"That doesn't sound like a big problem, Roxy."

68
00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.136
"I know," Roxy said.

69
00:03:45.137 --> 00:03:47.989
"But something big is behind the door.

70
00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.719
We need to know what it is.

71
00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:53.165
And since you can walk through walls . . ."

72
00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:54.582
Cozlin grinned.

73
00:03:54.583 --> 00:03:59.922
"Don't worry, Roxy. I'm on my way!"

